  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation through Economic Empowerment in Republic of Congo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Central Africa Regional):  USAID will use FY 2022 Biodiversity and Sustainable Landscape funds to address constraints to the growth of the green economy, aligning with conservation and forest management objectives in the Republic of Congo (ROC). The award will focus on stimulating private investment in green growth, spurring the establishment of local enterprises, and ensuring local communities benefit from forest and biodiversity resources. The activity will adopt an approach that actively improves the voice, rights and participation of women, indigenous peoples and other vulnerable groups. Work under this activity will build the capacity of targeted ministries in ROC to understand and address local constraints, particularly as they relate to economic expansion in agriculture and tourism. Tourism also has the potential to generate revenue for protected areas, contributing to counter wildlife trafficking, while agricultural interventions can assist in reducing demand for wildlife as a protein source..This activity will contribute to maintaining the ecological integrity of the humid forest ecosystem of the Congo Basin, which is vital to regional stability in Central Africa, a U.S. foreign policy priority. It contributes to Joint Strategic Plan Strategic Objective 2.2: (Promote healthy, educated and productive populations in partner countries to drive inclusive and sustainable development, open new markets and support U.S. prosperity and security objectives) by protecting natural resources critical to long term, sustainable growth, and food and water security. Furthermore, this activity will build the capacity of the government of ROC to meet its Nationally Determined Contributions for the Paris Climate Agreement and to access global climate funding mechanisms such as the Green Climate Fund and the Central African Forest Initiative, while also catalyzing private sector investment in low emission development..</narrative>
  </description>
